  "hint": {
    "id": "db/tables-empty",
    "matched_on": "checks[2].failures",
    "title": "The application's tables are there, but they are empty",
    "text": "Every table the checks read exists and holds nothing. Two causes produce exactly this. Either the dump was taken from the wrong database, or with `pg_dump --schema-only`, or narrowed with `--table`, so it carried a schema and none of the rows. Or the dump carried nothing at all and the application rebuilt an empty schema for itself on start, which is what an application with automatic migrations does the moment it meets an empty database. Compare the size of the dump with the size of the data directory in the report above: a forge with repositories on disk and a half-kilobyte dump is not a backup.\n",
